 "vyzhimka": {
  "tekst": "Yes. For a small LA service business dealing specifically with customers pushing back on price, I'd look for help with pricing strategy, sales process, and positioning—not just a generic business coach.\n\nA few LA options worth considering:\n\n- LA Regional SBDC — probably where I'd start. They provide no-cost, confidential one-on-one advising and explicitly cover product pricing, sales, marketing, management, and strategic planning. They have multiple centers around the LA region. ([smallbizla.org](https://smallbizla.org/services/?utm_source=openai))\n- SCORE Los Angeles — also free. They can match you with an experienced business mentor, and SCORE lets you search specifically for expertise in Pricing, Sales, Marketing Strategy, and Customer Service. ([score.org](https://www.score.org/ca/los-angeles/?utm_source=openai))\n- The DREAM Agency — a paid LA-area option that advertises positioning and pricing strategy for small and midsize companies. ([thedreamagency.org](https://thedreamagency.org/business-strategy-agency-los-angeles?utm_source=openai))\n- Insight to Action — another LA consulting option with explicit pricing-strategy work, though it appears more oriented toward broader growth/strategy engagements. ([itoaction.com](https://itoaction.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nFor your situation, I'd start with SBDC before paying a consultant. Tell the advisor: \"Customers regularly ask me to lower my quoted price. I want to figure out whether my pricing, packages, sales pitch, or customer targeting is causing it—and build a system for responding without automatically discounting.\"\n\nIf you tell me what kind of service business you run (cleaning, landscaping, contracting, photography, consulting, auto, beauty, etc.) and roughly what you charge, I can also identify 3–5 LA consultants/mentors who are particularly relevant to your type of business.",
